{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-340756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic extensions of some functions from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R$ with the Fourier series shown above. What is the $5\\text{th}$ Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340756" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi $-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x)+\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $-3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-3{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-3{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $5$th cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{5}-2{c}_{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Cour