\\beta g(x)∼\\frac{\\alpha {a}_{0}+\\beta {c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\alpha {a}_{n}+\\beta {c}_{n})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+(\\alpha {b}_{n}+\\beta {d}_{n})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $3f(x)-2g(x)$ are\n\n- $3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $3{a}_{n}-2{c}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $3{b}_{n}-2{d}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the $4$th sine coefficient of $3f(x)-2g(x)$ is\n\n$$\n3{b}_{4}-2{d}_{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340766" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aa216e64ce4c7359463a76d1167acab42f18802fbfbb34ddb4e1322e354f254"} {"question" "q-340766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340766" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3{a}_{0}-2{c}_{0}"] ["math" "3{a}_{4}-2{c}_{4}"] ["math" "3{b}_{0}-2{d}_{0}"] ["math" "3{b}_{4}-2{c}_{4}"] ["math" "3{b}_{4}-2{d}_{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340766"