 }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nRecall that if $C$ is a constant, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $f(x)+C$ are\n\n- ${a}_{0}+2C$  for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ${a}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ${b}_{n},$ $n\\ge 1,$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nIn our case, $C=1.$ Therefore, the constant Fourier coefficient of $f(x)+1$ is ${a}_{0}+2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aa216e64ce4c7359463a76d1167acab42f18802fbfbb34ddb4e1322e354f254"} {"question" "q-340778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{a}_{0}"] ["math" "{a}_{0}+1"] ["math" "{a}_{0}+2"] ["math" "{a}_{0}-1"] ["math" "{a}_{0}-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{a}_{0}+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-captu