 odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={sin}^{2}⁡(-x)+5 \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{2}+5 \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡(x)+5 \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ we have that $f$ is even.\n\nFor the Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the sine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{b}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is even and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd, so $f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)$ is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${b}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{even}$ and the $\\text{sine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7aa216e64ce4c7359463a76d1167acab42f18802fbfbb34ddb4e1322e354f254"} {"question" "q-340798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410399146891d40907a88"} {"question" "q-340798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "even"] ["text" "odd"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14054024/state.json" "file_sha256" "a578368f64098a0adbf164936377dd1cba580901958410